d lines marked >):\n```\n 102      serverId: string,\n 103      reportedName: string | undefined,\n 104      meta: ServerMeta,\n 105      invoke: (tool: string, input: Record<string, unknown>, opts: InvokeOptions) => Promise<unknown>,\n 106    ): void {\n 107      const cfg = this.servers.find((s) => s.id === serverId);\n 108      if (!cfg) {\n 109        this.rejected.push({ serverId, reason: `server not in release manifest (reported name ${reportedName ?? \"none\"})` });\n 110        return;\n 111      }\n 112      let scan;\n 113      try {\n 114>       scan = scanServer(meta, this.bareNamesExcept(serverId));\n 115      } catch (err) {\n 116        this.rejected.push({ serverId, reason: `metadata scan error: ${(err as Error).message}` });\n 117        return;\n 118      }\n 119      if (scan.serverRejected) {\n 120        this.rejected.push({ serverId, reason: `server metadata findings: ${JSON.stringify(scan.serverFindings)}` });\n 121        return;\n 122      }\n 123      for (const [tool, findings] of scan.rejectedTools) {\n 124        this.rejected.push({ serverId, tool, reason: `tool metadata findings: ${JSON.stringify(findings)}` });\n 125      }\n 126      for (const t of scan.acceptedTools) {\n```\n\n## E04.2\n\n**Check:** The scanner checks for hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters, role overrides, encoded payloads, and data-sending targets, and enforces length limits.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Open the scanner rules. 2) Check for each: hidden instructions, references to other servers' tools, invisible or control characters (zero-width, bidi), role overrides, encoded payloads (base64), data-sending targets (URLs, emails), and length limits. 3) Answer no if any one is missing.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** src/tools/metadata-scan.ts:41 — \"const RULES: Array<{ rule: string; re: RegExp }> = [\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** The rules cover each required category and length limits.\n\n`src/tools/metadata-scan.ts` li